# Example environment variables for local development.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repo root (that is the file the scripts below
# load, via process.loadEnvFile — not `.env.local`). `.env` is gitignored, so
# never commit real secrets.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL — the repo builds and runs with none of them
# set. Each is an override of a default that already lives in committed config.
# They are left commented out on purpose: an empty `KEY=` copied into `.env`
# sets the variable to an empty string, which the `??` defaulting below does NOT
# treat as "unset" — it would break `registry:sync` and the apps/web build.
# Uncomment and set a value only when you actually need to override the default.

# --- Registry URLs -----------------------------------------------------------
# The shadcn registry has two URLs, both stored in registry.config.json (the
# committed source of truth). These vars only override that config locally.
# See AGENTS.md §7 "The registry's two URLs — location vs origin".
# Both are also listed in turbo.json `globalEnv` (with NODE_ENV) so Turbo keys
# its build cache on them.

# Public URL consumers install from — a /registry path on the docs domain.
# Edit this, then run `npm run registry:sync` to propagate it into
# registry.config.json, the docs, and the generated registry JSON.
# Consumed by scripts/sync-registry-location.mjs. Default: `.location` in
# registry.config.json. In CI this is the `REGISTRY_LOCATION` repo variable.
# REGISTRY_LOCATION=https://ui.digital.nsw.gov.au/registry

# Upstream that the apps/web `/registry` rewrite proxies TO — the registry's own
# Vercel origin. MUST differ from REGISTRY_LOCATION, or the proxy loops.
# Consumed by apps/web/next.config.mjs. Default: `.origin` in registry.config.json.
# REGISTRY_ORIGIN=https://nswds-ui-registry.vercel.app

# --- Chromatic ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Project token for the Chromatic visual-regression service. SECRET — do not
# commit the real value. In CI it is the `CHROMATIC_PROJECT_TOKEN` repo secret,
# consumed by the chromaui/action step in .github/workflows/chromatic.yml. No
# repo script runs Chromatic locally; set this only if you publish Storybook to
# Chromatic yourself (e.g. `npx chromatic` from apps/storybook).
# CHROMATIC_PROJECT_TOKEN=chpt_0000000000000000000000000000000000000

# NODE_ENV is intentionally not listed: it is managed by the tooling (Next,
# Vitest, tsup) and appears in turbo.json `globalEnv` only for cache keying.
# Setting it by hand in a dotenv file is an anti-pattern — leave it to the tools.
